            <ArticleTitle>Etanercept in the treatment of refractory SAPHO syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>62-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore the application and efficacy of TNF-α inhibitors in the treatment of SAPHO syndrome.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Two cases of refractory SAPHO syndrome were successfully treated with etanercept. And pain scores, laboratory parameters and functional index were used to judge the efficacies. Literature was also systemically reviewed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Both patients achieved marked clinical remission. There was no obvious toxic or adverse response.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Etanercept has rapid and definite efficacies in the treatment of patients with refractory SAPHO syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
